# QUARANTINED — one case, blocked on full XID validation in descent.
# By documented design (both generator lineages), guards classify non-ASCII
# LEAD BYTES (0xC2-0xF4) as conservatively identifier-start, with a
# match_xid_start full-decode validation step that the templates reference
# but do not currently generate. CORE's rule is true XID_Start, under which
# U+2192 (→) is not a name start. Columns and content are UTF-8-correct;
# only the guard *classification* is approximate. Tracked in
# core/TODO-CORE-PARSING.md; re-enable by renaming to .yaml once the
# validation step exists.

- id: symbol_start_is_prose
  desc: a non-identifier symbol after the pipe fails the element guard — prose
  udon: "|→arrow\n"
  events:
    - [Text, "|→arrow"]
